The agents' icons (issues #62 and #441, DESIGN.md §29.9)

These files show which tool an agent runs, next to its name. switchboard is not affiliated
with, sponsored by or endorsed by OpenAI, Anysphere or Cognition. The icons are their trademarks and
artwork, not covered by switchboard's MIT license, and are used under each owner's terms.
Each is the owner's artwork, unaltered. If an owner asks, its icon is removed and the
monogram comes back.

codex-light.png, codex-dark.png
  The OpenAI logo (the Blossom), OpenAI's trademark, used to mark agents that run Codex,
  an OpenAI service.
  Source: https://openai.com/brand/ (Blossom_Light.svg and Blossom_Dark.svg). The logo path
  is unchanged, in the clear-space box the guidelines prescribe, rendered at 256 x 256.
  Terms: https://openai.com/brand/#usage-terms

cursor-light.png, cursor-dark.png
  The Cursor avatar, Anysphere's trademark, used to mark agents that run Cursor.
  Source: https://cursor.com/brand ("Download brand assets", Avatars/Square/PNG/
  AVATAR_SQUARE_2D_LIGHT.png and AVATAR_SQUARE_2D_DARK.png), unchanged.

devin-light.png, devin-dark.png
  The Devin avatar (the symbol on a white or a black square), Cognition's trademark, used to
  mark agents that run Devin.
  Source: https://devin.ai/brand ("Download brand kit", https://devin.ai/assets/brand/brand-kit.zip:
  Brand Logos 2026/Devin/PNG/devin-avatar-square-white.png and devin-avatar-square-black.png),
  unchanged. The light file is also served on that page as
  https://devin.ai/assets/brand/logos/devin/symbol-light.png. The page offers these as the
  official logos of Devin and Cognition and states no other terms.

Claude Code's avatar is switchboard's own chat-bubble drawing, not Anthropic's icon, with "Claude"
written under it in plain text on the Inspector: Anthropic's terms allow naming Claude Code in
plain text only.
